<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n91221" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Πτολεμ-ᾱΐς</span></b>  (also <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Πτολεμ-αιίς</span></b> ), <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ΐδος,
				ἡ</span>, with or without <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">φυλή</span>, name of an 
			Att.
		 tribe, named after Ptolemy Euergetes I, ib.<i><span class="en">
			22.957.28
		</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
			964.16
		</span></i>, al., <i><span class="en">
			Poll.
			8.110
		</span></i>; <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b>
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐπὶ τῆς Πτολεμαιίδος . . πρυτανείας</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>IG</u>
					22.897
				</span></i>
			, al. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b> name of
			several cities, esp. of one in Phoenicia, now <u>Acre</u>,
				<i><span class="en">
				Str.
				2.5.39
			</span></i>, etc.:—<b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Πτολεμ-ᾱΐτης</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ου</span>, or
				<b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Πτολεμ-αιεύς</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">έως</span>, ὁ, <i>a
				citizen thereof</i>, <i><span class="en">
				St.Byz.
			</span></i></div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
